1
00:04:08,181 --> 00:04:14,181
The maximum force of the future.

2
00:08:16,363 --> 00:08:22,363
Mad Max is a adventure, action, thriller film directed by George Miller.

3
00:12:24,545 --> 00:12:30,545
In the ravaged near-future, a savage motorcycle gang rules the road.

4
00:16:32,727 --> 00:16:38,727
Terrorizing innocent civilians while tearing up the streets, the ruthless gang
laughs in the face of a police force hell-bent on stopping them.

5
00:20:40,909 --> 00:20:46,909
Max Rockatansky, played by Mel Gibson.

6
00:24:49,090 --> 00:24:55,090
Jessie Rockatansky, played by Joanne Samuel.

7
00:28:57,272 --> 00:29:03,272
Toecutter, played by Hugh Keays-Byrne.

8
00:33:05,454 --> 00:33:11,454
Jim Goose, played by Steve Bisley.

9
00:37:13,636 --> 00:37:19,636
Johnny the Boy, played by Tim Burns.

10
00:41:21,818 --> 00:41:27,818
Fifi, played by Roger Ward.

11
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Mad Max is a 1979 Australian dystopian action film directed by George Miller in his directorial debut, who
co-wrote the screenplay with James McCausland, based on a story by Miller and Byron Kennedy.

12
00:49:38,181 --> 00:49:44,181
Mel Gibson stars as "Mad" Max Rockatansky, a police officer turned vigilante in a
dystopian near-future Australia in the midst of societal collapse.

13
00:53:46,363 --> 00:53:52,363
Joanne Samuel, Hugh Keays-Byrne, Steve Bisley, Tim Burns and
Roger Ward also appear in supporting roles.

14
00:57:54,545 --> 00:58:00,545
Principal photography for Mad Max took place in and
around Melbourne and lasted for six weeks.

15
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
The film initially received a polarised reception upon its release
in April 1979, although it won four AACTA Awards.

16
01:06:10,909 --> 01:06:16,909
Filmed on a budget of A$400,000, it earned more than US$100 million worldwide in
gross revenue and set a Guinness record for most profitable film.

17
01:10:19,090 --> 01:10:25,090
The success of Mad Max has been credited for further opening
the global market to Australian New Wave films.

18
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
Mad Max became the first in the series, giving rise to three sequels: Mad Max 2
(1981), Mad Max Beyond Thunderdome (1985) and Mad Max: Fury Road (2015).

19
01:18:35,454 --> 01:18:41,454
A spin-off film titled Furiosa: A Mad Max Saga was released in 2024.

20
01:22:43,636 --> 01:22:49,636
The film explores themes of australia, petrol, baby, chain, dystopia.

21
01:26:51,818 --> 01:26:57,818
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
